/* MT bare- AVIF fallback — v1.1.0 (2026-11-11). BUILD ONLY.
 * Why this shape: MT Fluid Images never emits  for these images and
 * MT Page Cache skips picture-wrapped images (proven 2026-10-27), so a markup
 * rewrite is the wrong layer. This client-side swap runs ONLY in browsers
 * that cannot decode AVIF (Safari < 16.4) and rewrites bare  AVIF
 * references to sibling files VERIFIED to exist on 2026-11-11
 * (evidence/avif-siblings.md — HEAD probes, existence = image/* content type):
 *   - Full-size originals exist for every sampled image (7/7):
 *       name-png.avif -> name.png    name-jpg.avif -> name.jpg
 *       name.avif     -> name.jpg
 *   - Same-size WebP siblings are INCONSISTENT (present for the two logo
 *     PNGs, absent for every sampled photo JPEG) -> WebP is only the
 *     error-chain second chance, never the first choice.
 *   - Size derivatives (-768x512.avif etc.) have NO same-size original in
 *     any format (all stubs); their FULL-SIZE original exists -> derivatives
 *     map to the full-size original. Larger bytes for legacy browsers beat
 *     a broken image; width/height attributes keep the layout box (no CLS).
